sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): the release of a task VM as its own run, for a task start that failed or a group that ended without a cancel run. The same steps end a cancel (docs/cli/tasks/cancel.mmd).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · the end of a task start that failed
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_release
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the release
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-release
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>and its seed clone
  SW->>HUB: Remove the hub peer<br/>wg set · remove
  %%> Runs beside the step before it: Swamp starts both at once.
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - beside it, the claim's model key is revoked at the model router
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>slot free
    Note over GW: Delete the Node record
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the VM keeps its slot and its Node; the sweep releases it again
  end
